+/*!
+   \fn bool QCborStreamReader::isNumber() const
+   \since 6.13
+
+   Returns true if the type of the current element is a number, that is, an
+   unsigned or negative integer or an IEEE 754 half-, single- or
+   double-precision floating point (if type() returns
+   QCborStreamReader::UnsignedInteger, QCborStreamReader::NegativeInteger,
+   QCborStreamReader::Float16, QCborStreamReader::Float or
+   QCborStreamReader::Double). If this function returns true, you may call
+   toNumber() to read that value as a \c double.
+
+   \sa type(), toNumber(), isInteger(), isFloat16(), isFloat(), isDouble()
+ */
